      "headline": "Backpack Secures CFTC Approval for U.S. Derivatives Exchange and Clearing, Plans Perpetual Futures Trading for U.S. Users Backpack announced that it has received approval from the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission (CFTC) for its U.S. derivatives exchange and clearing operations, including a Designated Contract Market (DCM) designation and a Derivatives Clearing Organization (DCO) registration. The company plans to offer U.S. users 24/7 leveraged trading in crypto perpetual futures, with support for fiat and crypto collateral, cross-margining across positions, and access to Backpack's global liquidity through a unified order book. — link",
