      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Wintermute Warns Crypto Bear Market Isn't Over, Recent Selloff No Sign of a Bottom Crypto market maker Wintermute warned in its November 16 market report that the bear market is far from over, with Bitcoin falling 12.7% last week to around $65,400, below its 200-week moving average near $68,000. U.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs have recorded $1.9 billion in net outflows so far in 2026, compared with $21 billion in inflows in 2025, while stablecoin supply has shrunk by $14 billion to $16 billion over the past 30 days. Wintermute said recent liquidations do not signal a market bottom, as rebounds appear driven by short covering rather than fresh capital. The firm warned Bitcoin could fall into the $50,000s and would reconsider its defensive stance only if BTC reclaimed $68,000 alongside renewed ETF inflows. — link",
